		<content type="html"><![CDATA[<p>Bonjour Guillaume,</p><p>La commande ping localhost me retourne :<br />&#160; &#160; &#160;[postgres@jips ~]$ ping localhost<br />&#160; &#160; &#160;PING localhost.localdomain (127.0.0.1) 56(84) bytes of data.<br />&#160; &#160; &#160;64 bytes from localhost.localdomain (127.0.0.1): icmp_seq=0 ttl=64 time=0.030 ms<br />&#160; &#160; &#160;64 bytes from localhost.localdomain (127.0.0.1): icmp_seq=1 ttl=64 time=0.014 ms<br />&#160; &#160; &#160;64 bytes from localhost.localdomain (127.0.0.1): icmp_seq=2 ttl=64 time=0.015 ms<br />&#160; &#160; &#160;64 bytes from localhost.localdomain (127.0.0.1): icmp_seq=3 ttl=64 time=0.013 ms<br />&#160; &#160; &#160;64 bytes from localhost.localdomain (127.0.0.1): icmp_seq=4 ttl=64 time=0.014 ms<br />&#160; &#160; &#160;--- localhost.localdomain ping statistics ---<br />&#160; &#160; &#160;5 packets transmitted, 5 received, 0% packet loss, time 3999ms<br />&#160; &#160; &#160;rtt min/avg/max/mdev = 0.013/0.017/0.030/0.007 ms, pipe 2</p><p>L&#039;équipe système m&#039;assure que SELinux n&#039;est pas installé, ni un autre Firewall et que la configuration réseau est correcte.</p><p>Aurais-tu d&#039;autres pistes ?</p><p>Merci.</p>]]></content>
